<title>BELGIUM: EU Commission proposes suphur cuts in fuel oil.</title>
<headline>EU Commission proposes suphur cuts in fuel oil.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-03-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>The European Commission on Wednesday adopted a proposal to cut the maximum allowed sulphur content in heavy fuel oil to one percent by weight by January 1, 2000, a Commission spokesman told reporters.</p>
<p>The Commission proposal would allow exemptions &quot;in regions where environmental conditions allow&quot; and for industries which use sulphur scrubbing technology. The proposal will be sent to EU ministers for their approval.</p>
</text>
